Systems currently supported:
Atari 2600
Atari 7800
Colecovision
NES
Sega Master System/Game Gear
Gameboy/Gameboy Color
GBA
TG-16
Some Arcade - list below

Arcade Games currently supported:
Donkey Kong, Donkey Kong Jr.
Pacman, Ms Pacman, Pengo
Popeye
Galaxian, Frogger, Moon Cresta, Amidar, Turtles
Double Dragon 1&2
Paperboy
Green Beret/Rush N' Attack
Simpsons

Save states not completed for Gameboy or Arcade, should work on other systems. F6/F7 to switch save slots. F5 to save state and F8 to load

Fullscreen Mode - use F11

Can enter Game Genie codes in cheat menu (Under EmulationMenu or hit CTRL+H)
Only supported for Gameboy and NES currently 

Zapper support using mouse - Only for NES currently. Need to go under Settings menu and check option to enable.

Can change controls by system under Settings/Controls
Not all systems support 2nd player controls yet, mainly TG-16, Arcade cocktail controls, and Coleco P2 keypad.

Default buttons are:
Up - 'W'
Down - 'S'
Left - 'A'
Right - 'D'
Select - Tab
Start - Enter
B - 'K'
A/Fire - 'L'
Insert Coin (arcade) - F1 or select button on joystick
Button 3 in Double Dragon 2 - 'J'
Select character in 4-player Simpsons - 'E'
 
Some systems require BIOS file to be put in $USERDATA/BIOS folder.
Colecovision (may be optional in future, some games like Venture would freeze when skipping)
Gameboy/Gameboy Color has option to skip
Gameboy Advance will use replacement BIOS if the official BIOS doesn't exist. License in the rusr/mimesys/src/gba directory.
Q-bert (optional, but sc01a.bin required for speech sounds)


NES Mapper Support:
0,1,2,3,4,5,7,9,10,11,13,16,18,19,
21,22,23,24,25,26,32,33,34,47,48,
64,65,66,67,68,69,70,71,72,73,75,76,77,78,
85,87,88,95,105,118,119,159,184,206,
Total: 49

